{"title":"2017 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />), the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that there are infinitely many distinct pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> of relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735b4fd08c7f1e4d6d79c161a483417073efb9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85b4a5f389c4da2b8d2b22498db71d019317eb9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e22c9be9c6a80931d1cc1532043a8e03157cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^b + b^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b8390d5cd3cb13344c7bd1b4945cf7a36c4656b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67265ee7f4f72acdd2f3ee4e29c094832f573ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, m_2, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"11\" /> be a collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers, not necessarily distinct. For any sequence of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a1cca8643e39135a3792d2d2b2ffe959af57df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (a_1, \\ldots, a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> and any permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095a11d278599a8ef41ecaa13fd814d6ec4e26c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = w_1, \\ldots, w_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"11\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da2b6334b62a0a80483de87afa53f047ea8e391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" />, define an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-inversion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to be a pair of entries <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d85e21cfb9cabfbcb25a864136683112cd4282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_i, w_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478f5d7d31a103e7a383486cdf317eb599ac9ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i &lt; j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> for which one of the following conditions holds:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e7a57a108c19f542380b6fa1beb50678c4c673.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i \\ge w_i &gt; w_j,\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f549c84bc48a26d35304ddc3d5ea8ff3bfdda743.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w_j &gt; a_i \\ge w_i,\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> or\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d846c7956ec8bfa8606414225de394a6712e90fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w_i &gt; w_j &gt; a_i.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />\nShow that, for any two sequences of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a1cca8643e39135a3792d2d2b2ffe959af57df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (a_1, \\ldots, a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe719a9ba5369772ca2c411ea6826bb5101a514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (b_1, \\ldots, b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, and for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the number of permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da2b6334b62a0a80483de87afa53f047ea8e391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" /> having exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />-inversions is equal to the number of permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da2b6334b62a0a80483de87afa53f047ea8e391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1, \\ldots, m_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" /> having exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />-inversions.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a scalene triangle with circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> and incenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />; the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbe20733d24579adb2707e9dc19f5c01568a351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DM}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> cuts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350503b4142c19abeb151a93622b4de560e27171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MK$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be6143db684699bb45c0e8501dec42f54ff9a5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{IS}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />. The circumcircles of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e661bca3eee8bcb4ca7f7397c95df0559579b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle KID$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5dfe30f7f5e56377ffe96abd13aef18c2fa15f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MAN$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> intersect at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f22b669e4803ae525cf8120ca251e2eab025872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13a902eb6a24cf493a2732badd0d151fb4f7672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> passes through the midpoint of either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/a/37accb2c5c1d405b922e6c93e3aed4dab6f8baf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{IL_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/59022d090e8fc69955a1bd17801165650ba9722e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{IL_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: For any geometry problem whose statement begins with an asterisk (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />), the first page of the solution must be a large, in-scale, clearly labeled diagram. Failure to meet this requirement will result in an automatic 1-point deduction. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c04d38658b5f8a60604d5df20c21af40d5f796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> distinct points on the unit circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1dd4184b561ea747be652fc3dee7fc5e1c5103f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />, other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Each point is colored either red or blue, with exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> red points and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> blue points. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cbbeb5834997d74dbc44264f04660c2bf84077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5f6500d904b18c0eaf34da49a31bd3fb72d7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fb734096ba7000d06944c083ecf0914ecffef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> be any ordering of the red points. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> be the nearest blue point to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cbbeb5834997d74dbc44264f04660c2bf84077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> traveling counterclockwise around the circle starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cbbeb5834997d74dbc44264f04660c2bf84077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. Then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/368b6f971b418d731c62ff2cb59f51c527d22849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> be the nearest of the remaining blue points to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5f6500d904b18c0eaf34da49a31bd3fb72d7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> travelling counterclockwise around the circle from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5f6500d904b18c0eaf34da49a31bd3fb72d7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, and so on, until we have labeled all of the blue points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a645b2e3ce7be9a34ba7bb03d7d23c70828f206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1, \\dots, B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />. Show that the number of counterclockwise arcs of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f5ec346f03238a599256db88f13c1ee03da323.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_i \\to B_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> that contain the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is independent of the way we chose the ordering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd5923183f47ced16286af761cf668d4e38c6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_1, \\dots, R_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" /> of the red points.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d4a3d7f9e00ba4ad4d80289be98fe888e31448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{Z}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> denote the set of all integers. Find all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c60c289e0343a236653229b2132befdfeabd04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> such that there exists a labeling of the lattice points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bff28acc1833d92da131e793f36a99ac614a816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$( x, y ) \\in \\mathbf{Z}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"19\" /> with positive integers for which:\nonly finitely many distinct labels occur, and\nfor each label <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, the distance between any two points labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0dffdaf42ac3fcc014af64f984a34b3e2ad9519c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^i$\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d21982ba412c0bb4a7985798e81bc5b01ac0e43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{b^3+4}+\\frac{b}{c^3+4}+\\frac{c}{d^3+4}+\\frac{d}{a^3+4}\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"39\" />given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are nonnegative real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4abe7bf20216ec9e3321ea7820466944d15ad666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO\" title=\"2017 USAMO\">2017 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 USAMO Problems\">2016 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems\">2018 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017093318\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 480/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1273/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 82/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14971/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.486      1 -total\n 55.15%    6.886      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 43.34%    5.412      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15563:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017093318 and revision id 205237. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}